    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Royal Prussia was formed when the Prussian Confederation of nobles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> rose against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> in 1454 and the Thirteen Years' War ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn">Second Peace of Thorn</a> in 1466.</li><li>Until 1569 it kept its own laws, council and parliament, and only Prussians could hold its offices under the ius indigenatus.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> of 1569 integrated it fully into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>, and the partitions of 1772 and 1793 gave its lands to the Kingdom of Prussia.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a>, the Polish chancellor openly admitted that integrating Royal Prussia breached the law by violating the privileges granted in 1454.</p></aside>
    </section>

