ss="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1506</span><span class="rf-text">The Statute of Prussia brings many Polish legal solutions into the Prussian legal system</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1526</span><span class="rf-text">Sejmiks are established and the Prussian parliament takes its bicameral form; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a> becomes the ruling religion in Danzig, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elblag">Elbing</a> and Thorn</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1569</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> integrates Royal Prussia fully into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1772</span><span class="rf-text">In the first partition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> the Kingdom of Prussia annexes most of the former Royal Prussia</span></li></ol>
